WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.840
Brain imaging across 57 studies ties multiple sleep disorders to smaller thalamus volume. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 238. Caffinated coffee and dementia risk, a new jellyfish off alicante, and a week in review. Florida International University researchers, as science daily reported, combined adult imaging of disomnias, such as insomnia and sleep apnea, with parasomnias, such as sleepwalking. The pulvinar subregion, which directs attention and supports cognitive

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.160
of control, was particularly affected.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.700
People with parasomnias also showed structural differences in the posterior singulate cortex,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.360
linked to motivation and emotion regulation.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.520
The analysis did not find a consistent structural signature unique to disomnias, even as shared

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.380
anatomy tracked problems of focus.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.600
Senior author Matthew Sutherland noted that the shared patterns clarify how sleep problems

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.700
affect focus and everyday functioning.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:03.140
Leed author Catherine Croak stated that looking across many studies revealed shared brain patterns tied to reaction times and errors.

00:01:04.132 --> 00:01:09.832
Drinking two to three cups of caffeinated coffee each day was associated with markedly lower dementia incidence.

00:01:10.352 --> 00:01:17.972
Follow-up in that work stretched up to 43 years. The same intake correlated with better cognitive performance across the follow-up period.

00:01:18.492 --> 00:01:22.312
Those associations appeared regardless of genetic risk factors for dementia.

00:01:22.312 --> 00:01:28.092
Decafinated coffee showed no comparable association with reduced risk or improved cognition.

00:01:29.237 --> 00:01:35.077
Coppula, Lucentia, was formally described in a Fizz.org report as a jellyfish only a few

00:01:35.077 --> 00:01:38.257
millimeters long from specimens collected near El Campello.

00:01:38.977 --> 00:01:43.957
University of Alicante researchers identified the species through work at the Ramón Margalef

00:01:43.957 --> 00:01:49.177
Multidisciplinary Institute for Environmental Research. The Find adds to evidence that the

00:01:49.177 --> 00:01:54.848
Mediterranean still harbors undescribed marine life, insects numbering at least 14 million

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:57.968
species deliver pollination that other animals depend on.

00:01:58.448 --> 00:02:02.768
The same groups decompose waste that would otherwise build up in the habitats vertebrates

00:02:02.768 --> 00:02:03.228
occupy.

00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:08.628
They also create physical structures used by other animals, adding habitat complexity

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.068
those vertebrates live inside.

00:02:10.788 --> 00:02:15.068
The contributions extend to supporting animal health in ways that cannot be replaced by

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.248
simple prey biomass.

00:02:17.458 --> 00:02:21.778
Medieval Tronheim recorded higher-round-worm prevalence after deliberate public health

00:02:21.778 --> 00:02:22.818
measures were introduced.

00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:27.758
Those sanitation changes coincided with more infection in the population rather than

00:02:27.758 --> 00:02:28.018
less.

00:02:28.698 --> 00:02:32.558
The conditions created by the interventions appear to have favored parasite spread.

00:02:33.118 --> 00:02:35.318
The measures had been intended to improve health.

00:02:36.108 --> 00:02:41.468
University of Bristol, in conservative post-reporting, joined four partner institutions to form

00:02:41.468 --> 00:02:46.688
the UK Quantum Superconnector that converts laboratory quantum discoveries into companies

00:02:46.688 --> 00:02:52.348
and products. The program includes a National Skills Center open to researchers across the country.

00:02:52.928 --> 00:02:58.428
Applications in view include healthcare imaging, aerospace sensors, and secure communications.

00:02:59.008 --> 00:03:03.608
The effort aims to retain economic benefits from British quantum research within the UK.

00:03:04.368 --> 00:03:08.968
Professor Ruth Olton of the University of Bristol described the initiative as an opportunity

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:15.075
to connect world-class research with investment and industry partnerships. A plant derived

00:03:15.075 --> 00:03:21.115
compound according to Bioengineer.org, improve survival under stress conditions in the nematode

00:03:21.115 --> 00:03:27.055
sea elegans. The finding adds to efforts identifying natural products that modulate cellular stress

00:03:27.055 --> 00:03:33.549
responses in simple model organisms. University of Alberta Research, reported by Fizz.org,

00:03:34.089 --> 00:03:39.089
finds that correcting soil acidity crop by crop fails to protect yields over multiple seasons.

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:44.749
Treating acidity at the rotation level produced more stable outcomes for Western Canadian grain

00:03:44.749 --> 00:03:50.269
systems. William grooms documented rare wildcat presence in northern New Mexico

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:55.069
during his first field season. He deployed dozens of motion sensing cameras across

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:59.729
Carson National Forest as part of a two-year biodiversity study. The work

00:03:59.729 --> 00:04:03.509
examines how forest structure influences species presence in the southern

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:09.088
Rocky Mountains. University of Ottawa researchers proposed a 26.7 billion

00:04:09.088 --> 00:04:13.448
year-old universe without dark matter or dark energy. The framework matched

00:04:13.448 --> 00:04:17.808
several key cosmological observations in work published in the journal universe.

00:04:18.148 --> 00:04:22.128
The tests included consistency with Big Bang nucleosynthesis predictions.

00:04:22.768 --> 00:04:27.908
In one more finding, archived rodent toxicity data are being mined for compounds that extend

00:04:27.908 --> 00:04:29.648
lifespan in model organisms.

00:04:30.644 --> 00:04:35.144
Most people assume a sleep disorder leaves only next day fatigue that a single restful

00:04:35.144 --> 00:04:36.024
night wipes away.

00:04:36.584 --> 00:04:38.764
The thalamus is not an afterthought of rest.

00:04:39.344 --> 00:04:43.484
It filters sensory information before that information reaches the networks that hold

00:04:43.484 --> 00:04:48.764
attention. Filtering is how a brain keeps one signal in a noisy field and drops the rest,

00:04:49.264 --> 00:04:54.464
and that same gate participates in working memory. Error monitoring uses those gates too,

00:04:54.724 --> 00:04:59.804
so missed details and slower choices can come from the relay itself rather than from mood alone.

00:05:00.524 --> 00:05:05.684
Tracking personal sleep consistency with a diary or a wearable gives a record to take to a clinician,

00:05:06.184 --> 00:05:10.364
while laboratories test whether earlier care can limit further structural shifts.

00:05:10.364 --> 00:05:16.564
Protein engineering in a robot-run cloud lab, United States structural fire loss projections,

00:05:17.064 --> 00:05:22.304
and three-dimensional genome maps of lab-grown neurons occupied the past seven days, and

00:05:22.304 --> 00:05:24.184
each thread is still sitting where it landed.

00:05:24.764 --> 00:05:29.824
An AI cloud lab used robots and models to compress protein engineering from years to days,

00:05:30.344 --> 00:05:32.604
and that compression remains the status of the work.

00:05:33.244 --> 00:05:37.504
Separate modeling showed United States structural fire losses could nearly triple by

00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:41.064
by 2060, without added protections or climate action.

00:05:41.544 --> 00:05:43.804
A projection that has not been revised this week.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.184
Researchers mapped 300 plus three-dimensional genome

00:05:47.184 --> 00:05:50.864
structures showing lab-grown neurons retain embryonic features

00:05:50.864 --> 00:05:54.464
unlike adult brain cells, and that contrast still stands.

00:05:55.483 --> 00:05:58.563
Before we go, William Groom still has a second field season

00:05:58.563 --> 00:06:00.843
left in his two-year biodiversity study

00:06:00.843 --> 00:06:02.463
across Carson National Forest.

00:06:02.963 --> 00:06:04.783
That's Planetarian Daily for Today.

